  "passage": "A cinema replaced its old seats with modern ones. Before throwing them away, the manager offered some to local artists.\nOne artist used the seats in a public art piece. She arranged them in a park facing a blank wall. On the wall, she projected people's memories of movies they had watched there.\nVisitors sat in the old seats and listened to stories about first dates, family trips, and childhood weekends.\nThe seats had once faced a screen. Now they faced memory.\nObjects from public places can carry shared emotions. When reused creatively, they let people sit inside the past for a moment.",
